---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Install the Hearth Skill for Claude Code and Codex"
  description="Install the Hearth CLI and Skill in one command so your AI agent can work directly with projects, memos, and schedules."
  locale="en"
  path="/install/skill"
>
  <p class="text-ink/70 text-sm font-medium tracking-wider uppercase">Setup · Skill</p>
  <h1>Let your AI agent<br/>work directly in Hearth.</h1>
  <p>Install the Hearth CLI and unified Skill together. The installer detects Claude Code and Codex so the next session can use Hearth.</p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <pre><code>curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/withgenie/hearth/main/scripts/install.sh | bash</code></pre>

  <h2>What happens</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The <code>hearth</code> CLI is installed in <code>~/.local/bin</code>.</li>
    <li>Claude Code and Codex Skill directories are detected automatically.</li>
    <li>The unified <code>hearth</code> Skill is linked and the CLI is verified.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Example</h2>
  <p>Ask in natural language from Claude Code or Codex. For example: <em>"Turn today's PRs into a Hearth project and schedule tomorrow's review for 3 PM."</em></p>

  <h2>What it can do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Create and update projects and priorities</li>
    <li>Create, connect, and organize memos</li>
    <li>Schedule work and brief you on today</li>
    <li>Reflect changes instantly in the open Hearth app</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Uninstall</h2>
  <pre><code>curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/withgenie/hearth/main/scripts/install.sh | bash -s -- --uninstall</code></pre>
</Base>
